{
  "extends": "./tsconfig-base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "types": ["node", "mocha"],
    "sourceMap": true,
    /**
     * **Every specifier the test tree can reach the core by, mapped to the same source files.**
     * `"rman/cli"` was missing, so a spec importing it got the *built* copy from `node_modules`
     * while `"rman"` gave the source one - two module instances, two sets of module-global
     * registries. `rman info` then ran the build copy's `SystemInfo` while the plugin had augmented
     * the source copy's, and reported `Binaries: [Node]` with no npm. Add a mapping here for any
     * new subpath export.
     */
    "paths": {
      "rman": ["./packages/rman/src/index.js"],
      "rman/cli": ["./packages/rman/src/cli.js"]
    }
  }
}
